***What is being built***

The source can be used to build two components:
- `p4` CLI binary itself
- `Perforce API` 

Both components require OpenSSL (3.x). Depending on how you obtain OpenSSL build (from external source or locally) you may run into additional dependencies at some point.

***Linux***

Tested on WSL/Ubuntu 26.04

== Preparations ==

1. Get `jam`:
- `sudo apt update`
- `sudo apt install jam`

2. Install compiler tools
- `sudo apt install -y build-essential`

3. Enable Linux file metadata in WSL
- Open `/etc/wsl.conf` and add
```
[automount]
options = "metadata"
```
- Restart WSL

4. Get OpenSSL
- `sudo apt-get install libssl-dev`

* Build OpenSSL
** `git clone https://github.com/openssl/openssl.git ~/code/openssl`
** `cd ~/code/openssl/`
** `git checkout tags/openssl-3.5.9 -b build-3.5.9`
** `./Configure linux-x86_64 --prefix=/tmp/openssl-x86`
** `make -j$(nproc)`
** `make install_sw`

* Build OpenSSL release package
** `mkdir ~/code/openssl-package`
** `cd ~/code/openssl-package`
** `cp /tmp/openssl-x86/lib64/*.a .`
** `tar -a -cf openssl_3.5.9-linux-x86_64.tar.gz *`


Current version as of writing this is `3.5.5-1ubuntu3.7` (`apt-cache show libssl-dev`)

== To build `Perforce API` ==

1. Run `jam -sOSVER=26 -sGCCVER=11.4.0 -sSMARTHEAP=0 -sTYPE=pic -sMALLOC_OVERRIDE=0 -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sSSLLIBDIR=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/ -sSSLINCDIR=/usr/include/ -sPRODUCTION=1 p4api.tar` (for Release build)

== To build `P4 CLI` ==

1. Install additional link-time dependencies

As of writing, the version obtained using `sudo apt-get install libssl-dev` (`3.5.5-1ubuntu3.7` - OpenSSL 3+ with compression) depends on:
- sudo apt install -y libjitterentropy3-dev
- sudo apt install -y libzstd-dev
- sudo apt install -y zlib1g-dev

2. Run `jam -sOSVER=26 -sGCCVER=11.4.0 -sSMARTHEAP=0 -sTYPE=pic -sMALLOC_OVERRIDE=0 -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sSSLLIBDIR=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/ -sSSLINCDIR=/usr/include/ p4` (for Release build)

***Mac***

Tested on Mac 12.7

== Preparations ==

1. Get `command line developer tools` to get `git` etc. - start e.g. by running `git` in terminal

2. Install `MacPorts` or `Homebrew`

3. Install `jam`
- Use `brew install jam` or `sudo port install jam` etc.

4. Clone the repository - `git clone https://github.com/Inglobor/p4-cli-api-25.2.git code/`

== Build universal OpenSSL libraries ==

1. Clone OpenSSL repository - `git clone https://github.com/openssl/openssl.git ~/code/openssl`

2. Go to OpenSSL folder, switch to desired version (`git checkout tags/openssl-3.5.9 -b build-3.5.9`)

3. Configure OpenSSL Intel platform build (`./Configure darwin64-x86_64-cc --prefix=/tmp/openssl-x86 no-asm`) and build it (`make clean && make && make install`)

4. Configure OpenSSL Apple platform build (`./Configure darwin64-arm64-cc --prefix=/tmp/openssl-arm no-asm`) and build it (`make clean && make && make install`)

5. Merge both versions to universal build
- `mkdir -p /tmp/openssl-universal/lib`
- Merge `libcrypto` - `lipo -create /tmp/openssl-x86/lib/libcrypto.a /tmp/openssl-arm/lib/libcrypto.a -output /tmp/openssl-universal/lib/libcrypto.a`
- Merge `libssl` - `lipo -create /tmp/openssl-x86/lib/libssl.a /tmp/openssl-arm/lib/libssl.a -output /tmp/openssl-universal/lib/libssl.a`
- Copy includes - `cp -R /tmp/openssl-arm/include /tmp/openssl-universal/include`


== To build `Perforce API` ==

1. Run `jam -sOSVER=120 -sCLANGVER=14.0.0 -sTYPE=pic -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sOSPLAT=U -sPRODUCTION=1 -sSSLLIBDIR=/tmp/openssl-universal/lib/ -sSSLINCDIR=/tmp/openssl-universal/include/ p4api.tar` (for Release build)

== To build `P4 CLI` ==

1. Run `jam -sOSVER=120 -sCLANGVER=14.0.0 -sTYPE=pic -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sOSPLAT=U -sSSLLIBDIR=/tmp/openssl-universal/lib/ -sSSLINCDIR=/tmp/openssl-universal/include/ p4` (for Release build)

== To build `Perforce API` ==

1. Run `jam -sOSVER=26 -sGCCVER=11.4.0 -sSMARTHEAP=0 -sTYPE=pic -sMALLOC_OVERRIDE=0 -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sSSLLIBDIR=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/ -sSSLINCDIR=/usr/include/ -sPRODUCTION=1 p4api.tar` (for Release build)

***Windows***

== To build `Perforce API` ==

1. Run `jam -sMSVSVER=18 -sSMARTHEAP=0 -sTYPE=pic -sMALLOC_OVERRIDE=0 -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sUSE_WILDARGS=no -sSSLLIBDIR=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/ -sSSLINCDIR="c:\code\OpenSSL\openssl\include" -sPRODUCTION=1 p4api.tar` (for Release build)

== To build `P4 CLI` ==

1. Build OpenSSL for Windows


2. Run `jam -sMSVSVER=18 -sSMARTHEAP=0 -sTYPE=pic -sMALLOC_OVERRIDE=0 -sUSE_EXTENSIONS=0 -sUSE_WILDARGS=no -sSSLLIBDIR=c:\code\OpenSSL\openssl -sSSLINCDIR="c:\code\OpenSSL\openssl\include" p4` (for Release build)
